.TH TULPAR-INSTALL 1 "2026" "tulpar 0.5.0" "Tulpar Manual"
.SH NAME
tulpar-install \- install one or more packages
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tulpar install
.RI [ options "] " package " [" package "...]"
.br
.B tulpar i
.RI [ options "] " package " [" package "...]"
.br
.B tulpar \-i
.RI [ options "] " package " [" package "...]"
.SH DESCRIPTION
Installs one or more packages. Each
.I package
argument is one of:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
a bare package name, resolved against the configured repositories
.IP \(bu 2
a path to a local
.B .apg
archive
.IP \(bu 2
an
.B http://
,
.B https://
, or
.B ftp://
URL to a
.B .apg
file, downloaded directly to the package cache, bypassing the
configured repository list entirely
.IP \(bu 2
a git repository URL (prefixed with
.BR git+ ,
or a plain URL ending in
.BR .git ),
optionally suffixed with
.RI # ref
to select a branch, tag, or commit. The repository is cloned and must
contain an already-unpacked package tree at its root
.RI ( metadata.json ,
.B data/
,
.BR scripts/ )
rather than a built
.B .apg
archive; intended for local development and testing workflows
.RE
.PP
Dependencies are resolved transitively against each package's declared
dependency list using libapg's dependency graph, and missing
dependencies are downloaded from the configured repositories before
the transaction is prepared. The resolved plan is printed and
confirmed before anything is written to disk.
.PP
Before asking for confirmation, the free space of the target
filesystem is compared with an estimate of what the transaction needs:
the installed files, the temporary unpacking of the largest package,
and a backup of the files being replaced. The estimate is conservative.
If it exceeds the free space, a warning with both sizes is printed and
confirmation is asked again; with
.B \-\-yes
the transaction continues without asking, and with
.B \-\-dry\-run
only the warning is printed.
.PP
If a requested package is already installed, it is upgraded when the
repositories, archive, or URL provide a newer version, in the same way as
.BR tulpar\-upgrade (1).
When the installed version is the same, the package is reported as
already installed, and nothing is downloaded if it was requested by
name; when the installed version is newer, the request
is skipped with a warning. If nothing is left to do, no confirmation is
asked.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-dest " " \fIpath\fR
Install into an alternate root instead of the live system.
.TP
.BR \-y ", " \-\-yes
Skip the confirmation prompt.
.TP
.B \-\-require\-signature
Refuse to install any package whose signature cannot be verified.
.TP
.BI \-\-sign " sig-path"
Use
.I sig-path
as the detached signature for the package instead of the
.IR file.apg.sig
found next to it. Only valid with exactly one local
.BR .apg " file, URL, or git-url argument."
.TP
.BI \-\-provider " name=package"
When more than one package can satisfy a dependency or
.B provides
name, force it to resolve to
.IR package
instead of the default choice (an already-installed provider, or
otherwise whichever provider was added to the transaction first).
Repeatable.
.TP
.B \-\-nodeps
Install exactly the requested package(s) and nothing else: skip
resolving, downloading, and queuing transitive dependencies entirely.
The underlying transaction may still refuse to commit if libapg's own
dependency graph considers the result broken.
Each dependency that is skipped and not already installed is reported
with a warning naming the package that depends on it.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-dry\-run
Resolve and print the transaction plan, verify package signatures if
required, then stop without writing anything to disk. Skips the
confirmation prompt.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, non-zero if resolution, download, or the transaction
fails.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tulpar (1),
.BR tulpar-upgrade (1),
.BR tulpar-download (1)
